Proposed change to harness/wspagent_settings.json: close the claude.ai account link for blind sessions.
NOT applied to the repo and NOT installed. Review, then apply and install yourself.

What each change does (all key names checked against code.claude.com/docs, 2026-11-04):
- disableClaudeAiConnectors: true   settings-reference: "Turn off claude.ai connectors so Claude Code doesn't
                                     fetch them" (any file). In run 94b05224151ce3d3, the "claude.ai Claude Docs"
                                     connector connected and 10 more connectors offered authenticate tools.
- syncClaudeAiSkills: false          "Stop loading the skills enabled on your claude.ai account and stop downloading new ones"
- syncClaudeAiPlugins: false         same for account plugins
- disableBundledSkills: true         "Turn off the skills and workflows included with Claude Code" (the 17 listed skills)
- enableArtifact: false              Artifact tool off; "no file can turn it back on"
- deny "Skill"                       skills.md: "Disable all skills by denying the Skill tool"
- deny "mcp__*"                      permissions.md: matches every MCP tool (second line of defence if a server still connects)
- env CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_CRON=1     disables /loop and the cron tools (ScheduleWakeup/CronCreate)
- env CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1  no auto-update, telemetry, feature-flag fetch (also makes Remote
                                     Control unavailable). Note: also stops auto-updates for wspagent's claude.

Not covered by any documented setting: the account email in the session context, and the account's identity on
the requests. Only logging wspagent in without the claude.ai account removes those: run /logout as wspagent and
provide a Console API key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or an apiKeyHelper script). Per authentication.md, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
outranks a stored claude.ai login; interactive sessions ask once to approve the key.

Apply + install (settings.json is immutable, so chattr -i first):
  cd ~/repo && patch -p1 < harness/wspagent_settings_seal.diff
  sudo chattr -i /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json
  sudo install -o root -g wspagent -m 640 harness/wspagent_settings.json /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json
  sudo chattr +i /home/wspagent/.claude/settings.json
  sudo rm -rf /home/wspagent/.claude/skills/synced      # if a sync already happened; preflight FAILs on any skills
Then commit the patched harness/wspagent_settings.json (preflight and audit compare the installed hash against it).
Verify: make_run's preflight now runs `claude mcp list` as wspagent and FAILs unless it reports no MCP servers.

